From 625921073470a07f6de1c529d5c8f1b02be40411 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:25:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Mac HDR export round 2: start-of-export colour (build 582
 still orange at the start)

Source frames whose colour tags describe neither their track's space nor the composition's are retagged to the track's space
and read with that colour space explicitly (a stray CGColorSpace attachment can no longer decide); output buffers lose any
CGColorSpace attachment before being stamped BT.2020 / HLG. EditV2HDRTrace records the tags the first frames really arrive
with. The HDR colour check now runs first in review mode, on its own (hdr-colour-check.txt, own CI step, never skipped),
with an untagged and a BT.709-tagged take, a first-15-frames check, per-frame values and TRACE lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Py2rxoCcw28R6FBjPPp318
